  "title": "Visit Deletion Code Path",
  "updatedAt": 1793523339191,
  "answers": [
    {
      "id": "vtqxyuyi8quRH334",
      "productId": "openmrs",
      "question": "When a user deletes a visit in the patient chart, what code runs from the frontend request down to the database write? List the frontend function that sends the request, the server-side REST handler, the core service implementation, and the data-access method.",
      "generation": "g-b59a21",
      "kind": "grounded",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "Deleting a visit in the patient chart is a **void (soft delete)**, not a physical delete. The chain is: modal → `useDeleteVisit` → `deleteVisit` → `DELETE /ws/rest/v1/visit/{uuid}` → `VisitResource1_9.delete` → `VisitService.voidVisit` → `VisitDAO.saveVisit` (Hibernate update).",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "## End-to-end trace",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**1. Frontend UI trigger**\nThe delete button in the dialog calls `initiateDeletingVisit` from the `useDeleteVisit` hook [1].",
          "citations": [
            1
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**2. Frontend function that sends the request**\n`useDeleteVisit` binds the confirm action to `initiateDeletingVisit`, which calls the `deleteVisit` resource function and then invalidates the current visit / visit-encounter SWR caches [2].",
          "citations": [
            2
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "`deleteVisit` is the function that actually issues the HTTP request: a `DELETE` to `${restBaseUrl}/visit/${visitUuid}`, where `restBaseUrl` is `/ws/rest/v1` [3] and [4].",
          "citations": [
            3,
            4
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**3. Server-side REST handler**\n`VisitResource1_9` (registered for `/visit`) overrides `delete(...)`; it no-ops if the visit is already voided, otherwise calls `Context.getVisitService().voidVisit(visit, reason)` [5]. The resource is declared with `@Resource(name = ... \"/visit\")` [6].",
          "citations": [
            5,
            6
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Note: a `DELETE` hits `delete()`, not `purge()`. `purge(...)` is a separate hard-delete path that calls `purgeVisit` [7].",
          "citations": [
            7
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**4. Core service implementation**\n`VisitServiceImpl.voidVisit` just delegates to the DAO's `saveVisit` [8]. (The hard-delete equivalent is `purgeVisit`, which checks for encounters then calls `dao.deleteVisit` [9].)",
          "citations": [
            8,
            9
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**5. Data-access method (database write)**\nBecause the resting object is mutated/voided, the DAO work is a save/update: `HibernateVisitDAO.saveVisit` calls `HibernateUtil.saveOrUpdate(...)`, which flushes the voided visit row [10]. The true physical delete method is `HibernateVisitDAO.deleteVisit` → `getCurrentSession().remove(visit)` [11], but it is not reached on the normal UI delete path.",
          "citations": [
            10,
            11
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "## Flow diagram",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "```mermaid\n---\ntitle: Visit delete flow\n---\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant UI as DeleteVisitDialog\n    participant Hook as useDeleteVisit\n    participant Res as deleteVisit (visit.resource)\n    participant REST as VisitResource1_9.delete\n    participant Svc as VisitServiceImpl.voidVisit\n    participant DAO as HibernateVisitDAO.saveVisit\n    participant DB as Database\n    UI->>Hook: initiateDeletingVisit\n    Hook->>Res: deleteVisit(uuid)\n    Res->>REST: DELETE /ws/rest/v1/visit/{uuid}\n    REST->>REST: skip if already voided\n    REST->>Svc: voidVisit(visit, reason)\n    Svc->>DAO: saveVisit(visit)\n    DAO->>DB: saveOrUpdate (voided flag write)\n    DAO-->>Hook: response, then SWR cache invalidation\n```",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "## Summary table",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "| Layer | Symbol | Location |\n|---|---|---|\n| Frontend sender | `deleteVisit` | [3] |\n| Frontend caller | `initiateDeletingVisit` | [2] |\n| REST handler | `VisitResource1_9.delete` | [5] |\n| Service | `VisitServiceImpl.voidVisit` | [8] |\n| Data access | `HibernateVisitDAO.saveVisit` | [10] |",
          "citations": [
            3,
            2,
            5,
            8,
            10
          ]
        }
      ],
